// PSS v3.0 LRM — Example 96: Scoping and named sub-activities (page 170)
action A {};
action B {
  int x;
  activity {
    L1: parallel { // 'L1' is 1st level named sub-activity
      if (x > 10) {
        L2: {      // 'L2' is 2nd level named sub-activity
          A a;
          a;
        }
        {
          A a; // OK - this is a separate naming scope for variables
          a;
        }
      }
      L2: { // Error - this 'L2' conflicts with 'L2' above
        A a;
        a;
      }
    }
  }
};

Example 97 below demonstrates a name conflict between a local action-handle variable and a label of an
activity statement in the same named sub-activity. This is not allowed, as it would render the hierarchical
path L.a from action A’s scope ambiguous.
